---
import LegalContact from "../components/LegalContact.astro";
import LegalLayout from "../layouts/LegalLayout.astro";
import { legalDetails } from "../legal";

const sections = [
  { id: "agreement", label: "The agreement" },
  { id: "service", label: "Using Tearleads" },
  { id: "keys", label: "Keys & backups" },
  { id: "content", label: "Your content & sharing" },
  { id: "acceptable-use", label: "Acceptable use" },
  { id: "billing", label: "Subscriptions & billing" },
  { id: "ending-service", label: "Ending service" },
  { id: "availability", label: "Availability & warranties" },
  { id: "liability", label: "Limits on liability" },
  { id: "disputes", label: "Law & disputes" },
  { id: "changes", label: "Changes & general terms" },
  { id: "contact", label: "Contact us" },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms for using Tearleads, including content ownership, encryption keys, sharing, subscriptions, cancellation, and service responsibilities."
  lede="The ground rules for using Tearleads: what we provide, what you control, and the responsibilities we each have."
  sections={sections}
>
  <ul slot="summary" role="list">
    <li><strong>Your content stays yours.</strong> You keep ownership. You decide what to put in Tearleads and who you authorize to access it.</li>
    <li><strong>Your keys need a backup.</strong> Keep recovery material safe. We cannot reset your identity keys or decrypt your content for you.</li>
    <li><strong>Subscriptions renew until canceled.</strong> Cancel through Stripe or your app store. Deleting the app or a local identity does not cancel billing.</li>
  </ul>

  <section id="agreement" aria-labelledby="agreement-title">
    <h2 id="agreement-title">1. The agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Service (“Terms”) are between you and {legalDetails.operator}{" "}
      (“Tearleads,” “we,” “us,” or “our”), based in {legalDetails.location}.
      They cover our website, applications, and hosted Sync and Sharing services
      (together, the “Services”).
    </p>
    <p>
      By accepting these Terms or using the Services after being given notice
      of them and an opportunity to review them, you agree to these Terms.
      If you do not agree, do not use the Services. You must be at least 18 and
      legally able to enter this agreement. If you act for an organization, you
      confirm that you have authority to bind it, and “you” includes that organization.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> explains information
      handling. Agreeing to these Terms does not replace any separate privacy
      consent required by law. Mandatory consumer protections remain in effect
      regardless of these Terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="service" aria-labelledby="service-title">
    <h2 id="service-title">2. Using Tearleads</h2>
    <p>
      Tearleads provides device-first tools for working with your information,
      with optional paid Sync and Sharing. Available features can differ by
      platform, version, plan, and connectivity. Local functionality does not
      require a paid sync subscription. Hosted functionality requires the
      relevant service access and, where applicable, an active subscription.
    </p>
    <p>
      Subject to these Terms, you may use the Services for lawful personal or
      organizational purposes. We retain rights in the Services, our branding,
      and our materials, excluding your content. Software supplied under a
      separate license remains subject to that license; these Terms do not
      take away rights that license grants you.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are responsible for the devices, connectivity, permissions, and
      authorized activity needed to use the Services. Keep billing and contact
      information you provide accurate. Do not use another person’s identity
      or credentials without permission.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="keys" aria-labelledby="keys-title">
    <h2 id="keys-title">3. Protect your keys and keep backups</h2>
    <p>
      Your cryptographic identity controls access to your encrypted content.
      You are responsible for protecting your devices, recovery phrase, recovery
      QR code, private keys, and backup passwords. Anyone with your recovery
      material may be able to act as you and access your data.
    </p>
    <p class="legal-callout">
      We cannot reset your identity keys or recover encrypted content without
      the necessary keys. Losing your keys and every usable recovery copy can
      mean permanent loss of access, even if a subscription is still active.
    </p>
    <p>
      Keep independent backups of important information and verify that they
      can be restored. Sync is not a guarantee of permanent archival storage
      or a substitute for backups. An export may include only files available
      locally, not every remote file. Clearing browser storage, uninstalling,
      destroying a local identity, or losing a device can remove unsynced data.
      Contact us promptly if you suspect unauthorized service access, but do
      not email us your recovery material.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="content" aria-labelledby="content-title">
    <h2 id="content-title">4. Your content and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      You retain ownership of the content you create, import, store, or share.
      You give us a limited, non-exclusive permission to store, copy, transmit,
      and otherwise process content only as needed to provide the Services
      you request, carry out your instructions, secure the Services, and meet
      applicable legal obligations. This permission does not transfer ownership
      or grant a right to use your content for advertising.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our ability to process encrypted content is limited by the encryption
      design. The permission above does not give us keys we do not possess.
      It continues only as needed for those purposes, including retained copies
      and records described in the Privacy Policy after use ends.
    </p>
    <p>
      You must have the rights and permissions needed to use and share your
      content, including personal information about other people. You are
      responsible for choosing recipients and access levels. Authorized users
      may read, edit, download, or further share content as their permissions
      allow. Removing access cannot erase copies or keys already received,
      and retained history may be available to later authorized recipients.
    </p>
    <p>
      Organization administrators can manage membership, billing, and service
      access within their authority. Changes by an administrator, including
      removal from an organization or a subscription lapse, may affect your
      access. You and your organization are responsible for agreeing on content
      ownership and administration. We do not resolve ownership disputes merely
      because one party possesses a key or pays an invoice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="acceptable-use" aria-labelledby="acceptable-use-title">
    <h2 id="acceptable-use-title">5. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>Do not use the Services to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Break applicable law or violate intellectual property, privacy, or other rights.</li>
      <li>Distribute malware, commit fraud, threaten or exploit others, or facilitate child sexual exploitation.</li>
      <li>Access identities, content, infrastructure, or systems without authorization, or bypass access controls or billing restrictions.</li>
      <li>Disrupt the Services, overwhelm infrastructure, or interfere with other users’ access.</li>
      <li>Misrepresent your identity or authority, or use sharing and communications for unsolicited abusive activity.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      These restrictions do not prohibit activity protected by applicable law
      or rights under a separate software license. If you discover a security
      issue, report it to <a href={`mailto:${legalDetails.email}`}>{legalDetails.email}</a>{" "}
      without accessing other people’s data or disrupting the Services.
      This invitation does not authorize testing systems you do not control.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="billing" aria-labelledby="billing-title">
    <h2 id="billing-title">6. Subscriptions, renewal, and cancellation</h2>
    <h3>Prices and payment</h3>
    <p>
      Paid plans, included capacity, currency, billing interval, taxes, and
      applicable charges are shown at checkout. Our <a href="/pricing">pricing
      page</a> describes the standard plans; store pricing and regional charges
      may differ. A subscription applies to the organization or entitlement
      identified at purchase, not automatically to every identity or organization
      you create. Unless checkout states otherwise, subscriptions are monthly.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you confirm a recurring purchase, you authorize the payment provider
      to charge the disclosed amount and applicable taxes for each billing period
      until canceled. Plan or capacity changes may change the price and may
      involve prorated charges, as disclosed by the billing provider. We will
      give notice of changes to recurring prices before they apply and obtain
      additional consent where required by law.
    </p>
    <h3>How to cancel</h3>
    <p>
      For web subscriptions, use <a href="/manage-subscription">Manage
      subscription</a> to access Stripe with the billing email used at checkout.
      This route can be used even if you have lost your Tearleads identity keys.
      For App Store or Google Play purchases, cancel through that store’s
      subscription settings. Contact us if you cannot access the cancellation route.
    </p>
    <p>
      Cancellation stops future renewals after the current paid period; paid
      access generally continues through that period unless a refund, store
      rule, legal requirement, or suspension changes it. Cancel before the
      renewal deadline shown by your provider. Deleting the app, removing a
      local identity, leaving an organization, or ceasing to use the Services
      does not cancel a subscription.
    </p>
    <h3>Refunds and failed payments</h3>
    <p>
      Except where required by law or expressly offered at purchase, payments
      for the current billing period are non-refundable and we do not provide
      partial-period credits merely because you stop using the Services.
      Contact us about billing errors or refund requests. Store purchases are
      also subject to the store’s refund process. Nothing here removes
      statutory cancellation, withdrawal, refund, or service-quality rights.
    </p>
    <p>
      Failed payments or an expired entitlement may restrict hosted features.
      After the applicable grace period, remote organization data may be
      permanently purged. Reactivating billing does not guarantee recovery of
      purged data. Keep local copies and independent backups of anything important.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="ending-service" aria-labelledby="ending-service-title">
    <h2 id="ending-service-title">7. Ending or suspending service</h2>
    <p>
      You may stop using the Services at any time. Cancel any subscription
      separately, export information you wish to keep, and use the available
      deletion controls or contact us about remote records. Uninstalling or
      destroying a local identity does not erase all remote information.
      Retention and deletion limits are explained in the Privacy Policy.
    </p>
    <p>
      We may restrict or suspend hosted access for a material breach of these
      Terms, nonpayment, a legal requirement, or a credible security or abuse
      risk. Where reasonably practicable and lawful, we will explain the reason
      and offer an opportunity to address it. Urgent threats or legal restrictions
      may require action without advance notice. You may contact us to ask for review.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we discontinue a paid hosted service for reasons unrelated to your
      breach, we will give reasonable advance notice where practicable and
      refund prepaid fees for the unused discontinued portion. We will provide
      a reasonable opportunity to export available data where technically
      feasible and lawful. Ending hosted access does not let us erase copies
      already on your devices or guarantee that remote-only data remains recoverable.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="availability" aria-labelledby="availability-title">
    <h2 id="availability-title">8. Availability and warranties</h2>
    <p>
      We work to provide useful, reliable, and secure Services, but outages,
      bugs, compatibility changes, network failures, and data loss are possible.
      Encryption has limits, particularly on compromised devices or when keys
      are exposed. Unless separately agreed in writing, we do not promise an
      uptime level, uninterrupted access, or permanent storage of every version
      or attachment. The Services are not designed for emergency or safety-critical use.
    </p>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, the Services are provided
      “as is” and “as available,” without implied warranties of merchantability,
      fitness for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. This does not
      exclude an express commitment in these Terms or any warranty, guarantee,
      reasonable-care obligation, or consumer remedy that the law does not allow
      us to exclude.
    </p>
    <p>
      Third-party stores, payment systems, devices, and services have their own
      terms. Their outages or decisions can affect your use of Tearleads. Their
      terms do not displace your mandatory rights against us.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="liability" aria-labelledby="liability-title">
    <h2 id="liability-title">9. Limits on liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the extent permitted by applicable law, Tearleads is not liable for
      indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or
      lost profits, arising from the Services. Our total liability arising
      from or relating to the Services is limited to the greater of US $100
      or the amount you paid us for the affected Services in the 12 months
      before the event giving rise to the claim.
    </p>
    <p>
      These exclusions and limits do not apply to fraud, willful misconduct,
      gross negligence, death or personal injury caused by negligence, or any
      liability that cannot lawfully be limited or excluded. They do not reduce
      mandatory consumer remedies or privacy rights. Where local law does not
      permit a particular limitation, that limitation does not apply to you.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="disputes" aria-labelledby="disputes-title">
    <h2 id="disputes-title">10. Governing law and disputes</h2>
    <p>
      Tennessee law governs these Terms, without its conflict-of-laws rules,
      except that mandatory protections of the law where you live continue to
      apply. Courts with jurisdiction in Hamilton County, Tennessee may hear
      disputes. This is not an exclusive venue requirement and does not prevent
      you from bringing a claim in another court where applicable law permits it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Please contact us if there is a problem so we can try to resolve it.
      Doing so is not a condition of exercising your legal rights and does not
      shorten or extend a legal deadline. These Terms do not require private
      arbitration or waive your right to participate in a class action.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="changes" aria-labelledby="changes-title">
    <h2 id="changes-title">11. Changes and general terms</h2>
    <p>
      We may update the Services and these Terms. Revised Terms will have a new
      effective date, and we will give reasonable advance notice of material
      changes through the Services or another appropriate channel. Changes
      needed urgently for security, legal compliance, or to introduce an
      optional feature may take effect sooner. We will obtain acceptance where
      required by law; changes will not retroactively alter an existing dispute.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you do not agree to revised Terms, stop using the affected Services
      and cancel any applicable subscription before the next renewal. Any
      refund rights required by law remain available.
    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms and any separate written service agreement form our agreement
      about the Services. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining
      provisions continue to apply. A failure to enforce a provision is not a
      waiver. Neither party may transfer this agreement in a way that reduces
      the other party’s mandatory rights; we may transfer it with a merger or
      sale of the relevant business if the successor assumes our obligations.
      Provisions that by their nature must continue, including accrued payment
      obligations, ownership, lawful retention, liability, and dispute terms,
      survive termination.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
    <h2 id="contact-title">12. Contact us</h2>
    <p>For questions about these Terms, billing concerns, or legal notices:</p>
    <LegalContact />
  </section>
</LegalLayout>
